She got Sheldon to go to a psychic with her.

266
00:13:09,150 --> 00:13:10,590
A psychic?

267
00:13:10,590 --> 00:13:12,690
He considers them not just mumbo jumbo,

268
00:13:12,690 --> 00:13:16,200
but extra-jumbo mumbo jumbo.

269
00:13:16,680 --> 00:13:18,880
Well, Penny can be pretty persuasive.

270
00:13:18,880 --> 00:13:21,750
She's gotten me to do a lot of things I wouldn't normally do.

271
00:13:21,750 --> 00:13:23,140
Because she has sex with you.

272
00:13:23,140 --> 00:13:25,630
Yeah, she does.

273
00:13:26,460 --> 00:13:28,430
Can I confess something?

274
00:13:28,430 --> 00:13:29,940
Once in a while, I get a little jealous

275
00:13:29,940 --> 00:13:32,090
of how close Penny and Sheldon are.

276
00:13:32,090 --> 00:13:33,510
Really?

277
00:13:33,510 --> 00:13:35,110
I mean, not in a romantic way.

278
00:13:35,110 --> 00:13:38,230
It's just, she really has some sort of connection with him.

279
00:13:38,230 --> 00:13:40,870
Well... Well, they've known each other a long time,

280
00:13:41,750 --> 00:13:43,190
and Penny grew up around horses,

281
00:13:43,190 --> 00:13:46,630
so she knows how to approach him without making him skittish.

282
00:13:47,430 --> 00:13:49,100
Don't get me wrong. I'm glad they're friends.

283
00:13:49,100 --> 00:13:52,580
I just wish he'd be that comfortable around me already.

284
00:13:52,580 --> 00:13:56,320
Well, it took him a long time to get comfortable around me, too.

285
00:13:56,320 --> 00:13:58,370
Really? What did you do?

286
00:13:58,370 --> 00:14:01,890
Something terrible in a former life? I don't know.

287
00:14:03,670 --> 00:14:04,410
I gotta go.

288
00:14:04,410 --> 00:14:05,700
Penny ratted me out.

289
00:14:05,700 --> 00:14:07,750
FYI, she's getting you a watch for your birthday

290
00:14:07,750 --> 00:14:10,140
with money she took out of your wallet.

291
00:14:15,990 --> 00:14:18,780
I don't mean to be rude or discourteous,

292
00:14:18,780 --> 00:14:21,260
but before we begin, I'd just like to say

293
00:14:21,260 --> 00:14:23,870
there is absolutely no scientific evidence

294
00:14:23,870 --> 00:14:26,420
to support clairvoyance of any kind.

295
00:14:27,050 --> 00:14:28,090
Which means--

296
00:14:28,090 --> 00:14:30,750
and again, no insult intended--

297
00:14:30,750 --> 00:14:32,560
but you're a fraud...

298
00:14:33,530 --> 00:14:35,460
...your profession is a swindle,

299
00:14:35,460 --> 00:14:37,520
and, uh, your livelihood is dependent

300
00:14:37,520 --> 00:14:40,100
on the gullibility of stupid people.

301
00:14:41,620 --> 00:14:43,910
Again, no offense.

302
00:14:43,910 --> 00:14:46,230
All right, Sheldon, just ask your question.

303
00:14:49,100 --> 00:14:51,960
Okay, I just did. What was it?

304
00:14:52,550 --> 00:14:53,270
Oh, for God's sake.

305
00:14:53,270 --> 00:14:54,890
Look, he's a physicist who's trying to figure out

306
00:14:54,890 --> 00:14:56,660
what his next field of study should be.

307
00:14:56,660 --> 00:14:57,720
For your information,

308
00:14:57,720 --> 00:15:01,010
I was asking her about the next Star Trek movie.

309
00:15:01,010 --> 00:15:04,020
Okay, I can answer that one: I'll be bored.

310
00:15:04,710 --> 00:15:07,690
All right, why don't we begin?

311
00:15:14,560 --> 00:15:17,200
Your spirit guides are telling me that

312
00:15:17,200 --> 00:15:20,870
there's a woman in your life you're having problems with.

313
00:15:20,870 --> 00:15:22,960
That's an easy guess.

314
00:15:22,960 --> 00:15:24,590
I'm clearly an annoying person

315
00:15:24,590 --> 00:15:27,410
and have problems with both genders.

316
00:15:27,410 --> 00:15:30,690
Yes, you clearly are.

317
00:15:31,360 --> 00:15:34,210
But I'm seeing a specific woman

318
00:15:34,350 --> 00:15:37,170
that you're in a romantic relationship with.

319
00:15:37,170 --> 00:15:39,880
Oh, oh, here we go.

320
00:15:40,430 --> 00:15:41,500
Does she have dark hair?

321
00:15:41,500 --> 00:15:44,790
Yes! Yes! Your spirit guides are on fire!

322
00:15:45,440 --> 00:15:47,940
The majority of people have dark hair.

323
00:15:47,940 --> 00:15:50,350
Even you, at one time.

324
00:15:51,230 --> 00:15:53,300
Does she work in a similar field to you?

325
00:15:53,300 --> 00:15:54,480
Ha! The opposite.

326
00:15:54,480 --> 00:15:58,110
She's a neurobiologist, and I'm a theoretical physicist.

327
00:15:58,110 --> 00:16:00,650
My spirit guides can go suck an egg.

328
00:16:01,910 --> 00:16:02,910
They're telling me that

329
00:16:02,910 --> 00:16:05,180
you have difficulty being close with her.

330
00:16:05,180 --> 00:16:06,900
Oh, he does. He so does.

331
00:16:06,900 --> 00:16:08,470
What should he do?

332
00:16:11,810 --> 00:16:14,610
He should give himself to this relationship.

333
00:16:14,610 --> 00:16:15,580
Once he does,

334
00:16:15,580 --> 00:16:18,670
all his other pursuits will come into focus.

335
00:16:18,670 --> 00:16:19,920
Sheldon, do you hear that?

336
00:16:19,920 --> 00:16:22,130
I mean, Amy is the key to your happiness.

337
00:16:22,130 --> 00:16:23,310
Exactly.

338
00:16:23,310 --> 00:16:25,420
Personally and professionally.

339
00:16:25,420 --> 00:16:30,390
Everything will fall into place once you commit to her.

340
00:16:35,890 --> 00:16:37,530
You know what this is?

341
00:16:37,530 --> 00:16:39,710
Yeah, and I reserve this word for those rare instances

342
00:16:39,710 --> 00:16:41,390
when it's truly deserved.

343
00:16:41,390 --> 00:16:44,530
This is malarkey!

344
00:16:48,310 --> 00:16:50,080
Wow, you really struck a nerve.

345
00:16:50,080 --> 00:16:53,100
I've never heard him use the "M" word before.

346
00:16:57,880 --> 00:16:58,840
Here we go:

347
00:16:58,840 --> 00:17:01,420
House of a 1,000 Corpses.

348
00:17:01,420 --> 00:17:02,820
Now, just so you know,

349
00:17:02,820 --> 00:17:04,780
I was a nanny for three years, so if you get scared,

350
00:17:04,780 --> 00:17:07,860
I can totally change your diaper.

351
00:17:08,830 --> 00:17:11,540
Actually, I have to tell you something.

352
00:17:11,540 --> 00:17:14,380
These kind of movies really aren't my thing,

353
00:17:14,380 --> 00:17:16,460
so, last night, I watched it

354
00:17:16,460 --> 00:17:18,170
just to see what I was getting myself into.

355
00:17:18,170 --> 00:17:19,090
Okay.

356
00:17:19,090 --> 00:17:20,400
And I have to be honest--

357
00:17:20,400 --> 00:17:24,010
I thought it was disturbing and weird,

358
00:17:24,010 --> 00:17:26,920
and it made me wonder what it says about someone who enjoys it.

359
00:17:26,920 --> 00:17:28,640
I wonder that, too.

360
00:17:28,640 --> 00:17:31,180
Then, why do you watch these things?

361
00:17:31,180 --> 00:17:33,500
Can I tell you something without you judging me?

362
00:17:33,500 --> 00:17:34,820
Sure.

363
00:17:35,310 --> 00:17:38,100
They kind of turn me on.

364
00:17:38,100 --> 00:17:39,880
And play.

365
00:17:52,780 --> 00:17:54,140
Hello.

366
00:17:54,140 --> 00:17:56,530
I didn't expect you this evening.

367
00:17:56,530 --> 00:17:57,900
Well, I was just feeling so bad

368
00:17:57,900 --> 00:17:59,700
about lying to you the other night,

369
00:18:00,550 --> 00:18:02,450
I wanted to make it up to you.

370
00:18:02,450 --> 00:18:05,730
And how do you propose to do that?

371
00:18:16,470 --> 00:18:18,720
Unless you have Gravity on Blu-ray under that skirt,

372
00:18:18,720 --> 00:18:21,750
I don't know where you're going with this.

